      <bibl xml:id="work-5537" type="lawd:ConceptualWork">
        <title xml:id="name5537-1" xml:lang="en" srophe:tags="#syriaca-headword" resp="http://syriaca.org">Hymn 8 on the Nativity</title>
        <author ref="http://syriaca.org/person/13" source="#bib5537-1" xml:lang="en">Ephrem — <foreign xml:lang="syr">ܐܦܪܝܡ</foreign>
        </author>
        <idno type="URI">http://syriaca.org/work/5537</idno>
        <note source="#bib5537-2" corresp="http://syriaca.org/nhsl http://syriaca.org/bible" xml:lang="en" type="abstract" resp="http://syriaca.org" >
          The hymn employs the theme of kenosis, God's incarnate accomodation to human limitations and sinfulness. Syriac Christian imagery brings the hymn from incarnation to soteriology, and concludes with praises for social groups such as unmarried girls, children, and brides.</note>
